SECURITY BLOCKER discovered in mobile fingerprint UX: browser JavaScript
cannot access the actual TLS peer certificate. The fingerprint API and app
code travel over the same connection and may be controlled by an attacker;
storing/comparing its reported value is not cryptographic certificate pinning,
and comparison cannot authenticate a self-signed connection. Corrected UI,
CLI banner and documentation to avoid claiming otherwise. No new LAN listener
was enabled. Secure peer authentication, packaged desktop controls and real
phone testing remain OPEN; the PWA is not approved for release as secure.
